# Anything the droplet executes or systemd parses must be checked out with
# LF endings regardless of the platform it was committed from. A shell script
# with CRLF fails at the shebang with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M",
# and systemd silently mis-parses unit directives with trailing carriage
# returns. Both are checked out on Windows here and run on Ubuntu there.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.mjs     text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer   text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
